# Bug Fixes: Clean CIHI Notebook (Phillip lead)

- Bug 1: .loc[idx] used with an enumerate counter on a melted DataFrame
  - After df.melt(), index labels are not sequential (0, 1, 2); enumerate produces a counter that doesn’t match
  - Consequence: silently writes ci_low and ci_high values to wrong rows, corrupting output without raising an error
  - Fix Option B chosen by team consensus: iterate using .items() instead of enumerate, avoiding index label mismatch entirely
  - No need to reset the index after melt; iterating by label is cleaner
- Bug 2: CI string parsed to float before point estimate is extracted
  - Point estimate (mean value) is destroyed before it can be written back
  - Fix: write the point estimate back to the value column before the bulk pd.to_numeric conversion runs
- Warning 3: regex pattern only handles hyphens in CI strings; n-dashes and m-dashes not covered
  - Common in Excel exports; causes parsing failures on those characters
  - Fix: extend the regex pattern to include n-dash and m-dash variants
- Warning 4: if not match guard always passes because a no-match returns None, which is always truthy
  - Guard never actually blocks; bad values slip through
  - Fix: use pd.notna() to properly catch null/no-match cases
- Hardcoded years (2018, 2019, 2021, 2022): years 2023, 2024, 2025+ were not being picked up
  - These were treated as column IDs instead of value columns, silently dropping data
  - Team agreed unanimously to switch to dynamic 4-digit year detection via regex
  - Fix does not change existing functionality; it just extends coverage to future years
- Additional issues flagged: dataset name mismatches, hardcoded variable names that may not match actual data, O(n²) pivot logic, and stale function definitions from cells that were never re-run
- All 9 fixes applied by Philip’s AI; corrected function bodies copied verbatim into the respective cells
- Changes accepted in Philip’s IDE but not yet pushed to GitHub pending final review

